{
  "info": {
    "name": "Settlement Service",
    "description": "Every endpoint the service exposes, plus ordered scenarios that demonstrate its guarantees.\n\n## Setup\n\nSet the `baseUrl` collection variable. Defaults to `http://localhost:8080`; point it at your Render URL to run against the deployment.\n\n## How to use\n\nFolders `01`–`04` are the raw API, one request per endpoint, for poking at things by hand.\n\nFolders `A`–`G` are **ordered scenarios**. Run each folder top-to-bottom with the Collection Runner (or click through in order) — later requests depend on variables set by earlier ones. Each has assertions, so a green run is a real proof, not just a 200.\n\n## Scenario E is the one that makes `deduped retries` move\n\nIt stays 0 in normal operation because a downstream 500 records nothing, so an ordinary retry-after-failure never produces a duplicate delivery. Scenario E redelivers a settlement key the provider has already settled, which is exactly what a crashed instance or a post-commit timeout would do. Watch `deduped retries` go up while `double-settled` stays 0 — that is the whole guarantee in one step.\n\nFor the same thing arising *organically* rather than by hand, restart the app with the request timeout squeezed under the provider's latency so post-commit ambiguity is routine:\n\n```\nMOCK_FAILURE_RATE=0.0\nMOCK_MIN_LATENCY=50ms\nMOCK_MAX_LATENCY=600ms\nSETTLEMENT_REQUEST_TIMEOUT=300ms\n```\n\nRoughly half the calls then time out *after* the provider committed, every retry dedupes, and the counter climbs on its own. Those three are read at startup, so they need a restart — unlike the fault rate, which is tunable at runtime.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:8080" },
    { "key": "payment_id", "value": "" },
    { "key": "settlement_key", "value": "" },
    { "key": "amount", "value": "125000" },
    { "key": "idem_key", "value": "" },
    { "key": "deduped_before", "value": "0" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "01 · Health & Ops",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /healthz — liveness",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/healthz", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["healthz"] },
            "description": "Deliberately checks nothing external. A liveness probe that fails on a database outage turns a recoverable incident into a crash loop."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('status ok', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql('ok'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /readyz — readiness",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/readyz", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["readyz"] },
            "description": "Checks the datastore. 503 when Postgres is unreachable, so the instance leaves rotation."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('datastore ok', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().datastore).to.eql('ok'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /metrics — Prometheus exposition",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/metrics", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["metrics"] }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": ["pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "02 · Payments API",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "POST /payments — authorize",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Acme invoice #1041\",\n  \"amount\": 125000,\n  \"currency\": \"INR\",\n  \"idempotency_key\": \"{{$guid}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/payments", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["payments"] },
            "description": "`amount` is integer minor units (paise) — never a float. `name` is an optional label, max 120 chars, not unique, not an identifier. `idempotency_key` is required."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('payment_id', b.id);",
                  "pm.test('AUTHORIZED', () => pm.expect(b.state).to.eql('AUTHORIZED'));",
                  "pm.test('nothing queued before capture', () => pm.expect(b.settlement_state).to.eql('NONE'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /payments — authorize without a name",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"amount\": 7500,\n  \"currency\": \"INR\",\n  \"idempotency_key\": \"{{$guid}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/payments", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["payments"] },
            "description": "The name is optional. Omitted stays null and renders as an em dash in the admin UI — nothing is invented."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test('name is null, not a placeholder', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().name).to.be.null);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /payments/{id}",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/payments/{{payment_id}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["payments", "{{payment_id}}"]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": ["pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /payments — recent list",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/payments?limit=50",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["payments"],
              "query": [{ "key": "limit", "value": "50" }]
            },
            "description": "Backing list for the admin page. limit is clamped to 1–500."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": ["pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /payments/{id}/capture",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"idempotency_key\": \"{{$guid}}\"\n}" },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/payments/{{payment_id}}/capture",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["payments", "{{payment_id}}", "capture"]
            },
            "description": "Captures exactly once and enqueues the settlement job in the same transaction. Only AUTHORIZED is capturable."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (b.settlement_key) pm.collectionVariables.set('settlement_key', b.settlement_key);",
                  "pm.test('CAPTURED', () => pm.expect(b.state).to.eql('CAPTURED'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /payments/{id}/void",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/payments/{{payment_id}}/void",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["payments", "{{payment_id}}", "void"]
            },
            "description": "Moves an AUTHORIZED payment to the terminal FAILED state, so 'a failed payment cannot be captured' is a reachable path rather than a claim about an unreachable state."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "03 · Admin API",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /admin/stats — the correctness gate",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/stats", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["admin", "stats"] },
            "description": "One request that answers the whole gate. `invariants.safety_holds` is the pass/fail; the downstream counts are the supporting evidence."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const i = pm.response.json().invariants;",
                  "pm.test('safety holds', () => pm.expect(i.safety_holds).to.be.true);",
                  "pm.test('no payment settled twice', () => pm.expect(i.double_settled_payments).to.eql(0));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /admin/drain",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/drain?passes=5",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["admin", "drain"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "passes", "value": "5" },
                { "key": "batch_size", "value": "50", "disabled": true }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Drains the outbox now; the background tick runs the same code path. Safe to call concurrently with itself — that is what FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED is for, and doing so is a legitimate way to check nothing settles twice."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": ["pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /admin/dead-letters",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/dead-letters?limit=100",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["admin", "dead-letters"],
              "query": [{ "key": "limit", "value": "100" }]
            },
            "description": "Nothing is silently dropped: terminal failures are listed here for reconciliation."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /admin/mock-settlement/config",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/mock-settlement/config",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["admin", "mock-settlement", "config"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /admin/mock-settlement/config — pin fault rate",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"failure_rate\": 0.0\n}" },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/mock-settlement/config",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["admin", "mock-settlement", "config"]
            },
            "description": "0.0 proves convergence deterministically, 1.0 forces dead-lettering. Changed at runtime, no redeploy."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "04 · Downstream (simulated provider)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "POST /mock-settlement — settle a key",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"settlement_key\": \"{{settlement_key}}\",\n  \"payment_id\": \"{{payment_id}}\",\n  \"name\": \"Acme invoice #1041\",\n  \"amount_minor\": {{amount}},\n  \"currency\": \"INR\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/mock-settlement", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["mock-settlement"] },
            "description": "This is NOT your service — it is the simulated provider, reachable over real HTTP. It is idempotent on settlement_key (that column is its PRIMARY KEY), sleeps 100–500ms, and returns 500 at the configured fault rate. Its 500s mean 'not settled', so a retry is free to settle."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
